meta {
  name: Strategy: ML Trend Following
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/backtest
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "strategy_name": "trend_following_ml_strategy",
    "symbol": "SPY",
    "start_date": "2025-08-05T00:00:00",
    "end_date": "2025-11-06T23:59:59",
    "initial_capital": "10000",
    "commission_per_share": "0",
    "slippage_bps": 5,
    "config": {
      "model_path": "models/xgboost_spy_trend_following.pkl",
      "position_size": 10,
      "confidence_threshold": 0.6,
      "require_all_timeframes": true,
      "max_bars_buffer": 200
    }
  }
}

docs {
  Run a backtest for the Trend-Following ML Strategy (XGBoost classifier)

  Strategy Details:
  - Uses pre-trained XGBoost model with ~28 focused trend-following features
  - Predicts BUY/SELL/HOLD signals on 5-minute bars
  - Requires 1min, 5min, 15min, and 30min data for multi-timeframe slopes
  - Filters signals by confidence threshold (default: 0.6)

  Entry Criteria:
  - LONG: Bullish EMA alignment + strong slope + reclaim EMA20 + price > VWAP
  - SHORT: Bearish EMA alignment + strong slope + break EMA20 + price < VWAP

  Exit Criteria:
  - LONG exit: Price closes below EMA20 OR EOD (3:55 PM ET)
  - SHORT exit: Price closes above EMA20 OR EOD (3:55 PM ET)

  Features (28 total):
  - EMA slopes (16): EMA2/5/10/20 for 1min/5min/15min/30min
  - ADX values (4): 1min/5min/15min/30min
  - Alignment strength (4): 1min/5min/15min/30min
  - Bar reclaim pattern (1)
  - Price vs VWAP (1)
  - Time features (2): hour, minutes_since_open

  Returns:
  - Backtest ID and status
  - Performance metrics (total return, Sharpe ratio, max drawdown, etc.)
  - All trades executed
  - Equity curve points

  Date range: Test period (Aug 2025 - Nov 2025)
  Initial capital: $10,000
  No commission, 5 bps slippage

  Note:
  - Adjust confidence_threshold (0.5-0.9) to tune trade frequency
  - Expects stronger feature importance than original ML strategy (>10% vs 4%)
  - Bidirectional strategy (LONG and SHORT trades)
}
